---
/**
 * The idea behind the studio, stated plainly. Leads with the outcome (being
 * trusted), never the tooling. The credibility motif carries the section: for
 * a practice, the website is the first handshake, and trust is what converts.
 */
---

<section class="p-section p-manifesto">
  <p class="p-label" data-p-fade>01 · The idea</p>

  <h2 class="p-statement p-display" data-p-lines>
    <span class="p-mask"><span class="p-mask-inner">Trust is the</span></span>
    <span class="p-mask"><span class="p-mask-inner">whole product.</span></span>
  </h2>

  <div class="p-manifesto-cols">
    <p data-p-fade>
      For a practice, the website is the first handshake. A visitor decides in
      seconds whether you are careful, capable, and worth a call. We design for
      that moment: clear, calm, and credible, agreed in plain language first.
    </p>
    <p data-p-fade>
      From there it is steady and thorough. Real screens you can click, fast to
      load and easy to read, built to hold up under scrutiny and to keep earning
      trust long after launch day.
    </p>
  </div>

  <span class="p-rule" data-p-rule aria-hidden="true"></span>
</section>

<style>
  .p-manifesto-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    max-width: 920px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.6rem, 7vh, 4rem);
  }
  .p-manifesto-cols p {
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.3vw, 1.14rem);
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--p-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .p-manifesto-cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
